    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations by adapting to students’ strengths/weaknesses (e.g., my struggle with abstract math). Interactive tutors could break down proofs or solve problems step-by-step, reducing anxiety. For example, an AI explaining limits intuitively might help more than dry textbook derivations. But human oversight is key—LLMs should guide, not replace, critical thinking."
